From 1882cc69d48f46ecc83512d643a94e44fb1b4209 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Almaz Tleubay <almaz.tleubay@icloud.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:43:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fetch METR AI-progress data live on Refresh

Refresh now downloads METR's published time-horizon file, validates it,
and writes a new dated snapshot (ai_progress.csv, scenarios.csv, manifest)
when it differs from the newest saved one. On any failure it keeps using the
saved snapshot and reports why.

- backend/engine/ingest.js: fetch, parse, validate, write snapshot
- backend/engine/index.js: refreshData() uses it; one refresh at a time
- scripts: npm run ingest:check (read-only) and npm run ingest:now
- UI: Refresh messages and About page show live fetch time
- tests: 8 new (97 total), round-trip against the real 2026-10-23 data
